Spoilers follow

 
  The spoiler has to do with the fact that blessing/cursing bags
  of holding seems to be buggy. Basically what happens is that if 
  you take a bag of holding full of stuff, curse it, and then uncurse
  it, it's weight becomes negative! You can see this because you
  can pick up stuff till all inventory letters (a-zA-Z) are used.
  Then if you drop the bag of holding you collapse under your load.
  Pick it up, and you're walking around again. It is not necessary to
  put the stuff in the bag to able to carry it, all you have to do is
  be carrying the bag.

  When I did it, I filled the bag of holding with junk until I 
  couldn't carry anymore, then cursed it. I then removed everything
  (some stuff disappears) and uncursed it. Then I could carry until all
  my inventory letters are used (and more in the bag).

  I don't know if the bag needs to be full of stuff, then cursed, then
  emptied, then uncursed. I don't know if the apparent negative weight
  of the bag is related to how much stuff was in it when it was cursed,
  or how much stuff disappeared on coming out of the cursed bag, etc.
  That is, it might work with just an empty bag of holding without the
  intermediate steps of filling and emptying the bag. Anyone know?

  Another interesting bit: when I did this and was carrying the negative
  weight bag, I could also squeeze into all the openings on boulders, and
  I never got the "You are carrying too much to get through" message.
  Apparently these are both determined by the weight of stuff you
  are carrying.

  It's a neat trick. You can pick up dragon corpses, even with a full
  load (as long as you have an inventory letter for it).

  I think it is probably a (by now well-known) bug.

  One other bag of holding question: I stuck Stormbringer in the bag, and
  several turns later went to remove it. All that came out was a 
  blessed broadsword, not my Stormy! :( Anyone else ever have this 
  happen or know anything about it?
